    "crewed": false,
    "description": {
      "value": "<p>The target takes an extra 1d6 damage of the weapon's type. If the target is a creature, it must succeed on a Strength saving throw or have the &amp;Reference[Prone] condition.</p><p>Once per turn, when you hit a target with a melee weapon attack or a ranged weapon attack using a thrown weapon, you can imbue the attack with this effect. The saving throw DC equals 8 + your proficiency bonus + your Strength or Constitution modifier. You can use this feat a number of times equal to your proficiency bonus, and you regain all expended uses when you finish a long rest.</p><section class=\"secret\" id=\"secret-n6Lx8N5Y4v1nRhXQ\"><p><strong>Foundry Note</strong></p><p>Use the activity after a hit: it spends a use and rolls the extra damage and the saving throw. Choose the weapon's damage type when rolling the damage. On a failed save, the target gets the <em>Hill Strike</em> effect, which gives it the Prone condition. The once-per-turn limit is not tracked.</p></section>",
